# mix-of-capabilities §8.1 P2 — 10×23 su un caso pratico: un effetto con piu'
# cause (foglie gialle) riceve le cause candidate e la domanda sull'osservabile
# che le separa; la risposta dell'utente restringe a una causa. Fatti insegnati
# parlando e salvati (University of Maryland Extension; guide di cura).
[mock live]
!set PARROT0_SESSION=
!set PARROT0_PROFILE=kb/profiles/agi.p0
!set PARROT0_LANG=en
!reset

[test the candidates and the discriminating question, then the narrowing answer]
!timeout 30
> why are my plant's leaves turning yellow?
<~ Several things cause yellow leaves
<~ overwatering
<~ underwatering
<~ low light
<~ To tell them apart, do you see
<~ soggy soil
<~ dry soil
> the soil is soggy
< That points to overwatering: soggy soil is a sign of overwatering, which causes yellow leaves.

[test the other sign, said differently, points to the other cause]
!timeout 30
> why are the leaves of my basil turning yellow?
<~ To tell them apart
> the soil feels very dry
< That points to underwatering: dry soil is a sign of underwatering, which causes yellow leaves.

[test a third cause with a sign of several words can be pointed to]
!timeout 30
> why are my plant leaves turning yellow?
<~ leggy stems
> the stems look leggy
< That points to low light: leggy stems is a sign of low light, which causes yellow leaves.
